// Questions written in the voice of the real Weakest Link, researched from episode
// transcripts. Three devices recur, mirroring the show:
//   - "In [subject], ..." — the formal setup the host reads.
//   - Letter clues — the hint lands LAST ("..., starting with the letter M?"), so the
//     player hears the whole question before the help.
//   - Wordplay links — two unrelated things connected (Hush Puppies, the 49ers).
// Difficulty is mixed roughly 60/30/10 (gettable / makes-you-sweat / stumper): the goal
// of a round is a CHAIN, so easy questions are load-bearing, not filler.
// Every answer is short and unambiguous — the host judges by ear, there is no matching.
